  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Place a wall to get stuck into at 0,0,0.  Change the respawn point to a valid area in the build. \n\nAdd the Position Sync persistence example to the world. \n\nPlayers who have never visited the world before seem to work normally.  But players who have visited before, or players who reset their player data before coming back, appear to get stuck in the wall at a 0 position.\n\nThe only explanation I have for this behavior is that OnPlayerRestored is firing despite there being no data for the previously visiting players to load.  In other words, it's different from never having visited the world before, when it seems to me that wiping player data for a world should be identical to never having visited before. \n\nI can work around this, but this seems inconsistent to me.  I can provide additional debugging info in a few hours as well.",
